rows.en:
"Come on, let go!
Let me gooo☆"
And just like that, his consciousness slipped away..........{p}

Someone who happened to be passing by had found Nanase collapsed at the school gate and taken him to the hospital.
He... wasn't especially badly hurt, but for a while, apparently, he was in a state of suspended animation...
Right around the time his mother heard his voice.{p}

When he stole a look inside through the window, everyone was listening intently to a lesson.
...Looks like there's a class going on.
What kind of class could they be having at this hour?{p}

Heh heh...
He was frozen stiff with fear, you see.
Though he insists he was just watching to see what would happen.{p}

I see...
So you're the type whose body moves before you think, {a}.
Nanase was the same.{p}

"Wh-whoaaa!"
His legs nearly gave out, but Nanase desperately got to his feet and started running again.
And then the soldier came after him, clattering and clunking all the way.{p}

...{a}?
Do you seriously think that?
Do you really think anyone would charge at a ghost, just because they can't get away?{p}

...I see.
You don't want to go that badly.
Oh well, it can't be helped.{p}

With those words, Iwashita disappeared into the darkness at the far end of the hallway.
"Well then, everyone, shall we go back to the club room?"
We left the old school building, leaving Iwashita behind.{p}

"It can't be...☆"
Everyone broke into a run at once.
Toward the old school building, where the voice had come from...{p}

That's awful...
A girl staying alone? That's dangerous!
...That's what they were all saying, and yet.{p}
